Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 21:16:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/24] Test unsyncable retirement against durable-commit
 refusal and sticky failures

A WAL directory that cannot sync now fails the first durable commit before
it writes (decision 9): the files stay byte for byte, reads work and later
writes are refused with the recorded failure, so nothing is retired or
reused. A shared connection keeps a checkpoint's stopped-syncing failure
until it is reopened (decision 6, default C); a new connection recovers and
commits durably.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
